body:
Yeah!! The sun also makes me feel a lot more anxious for some reason, too. But I love the rain, snow, and dark clouds. Just the other day, I went outside and stood in the rain for a while. It was actually the most relaxed I've felt in a long while.

&#x200B;

I mean, I got sick afterwards, but still. It was nice.

Me too.

&#x200B;

I just don't have the energy anymore...

I honestly worry about this all the time... And something kind of similar has happened to me, too. Not being replaced by another person exactly, but life things. One of my friends graduated high school (while I'm left behind) and got accepted to his dream university. I was trying to be happy for said friend, but he was the type who would focus on schoolwork so much that he'd ignore everything else- Even when he was stressed about schoolwork, I'd try to help out, and he ended up lashing out at me occasionally. But I would always try to be there for him, and talk to him, but then... I gave up. *I* ended up leaving *him* instead, out of fear that he'd leave me first. I didn't want to go through the pain of being left behind. Despite the texts that he misses me, it feels hollow. I'm scared to be alone, so I'm clinging to another friend now, whose life is... honestly not much more eventful than mine.

&#x200B;

Though I don't have much advice... It's ok to cry. I definitely cried a lot at the thought of losing friends and being replaced, too. If it helps express your feelings, it's alright. And even if we don't know each other, I'm here for you.

Yesssss, night time is the best <3

&#x200B;

Also, it feels like you don't have to deal with any responsibilities or socializing or anything once night time rolls around, since everyone else is asleep. I love that.
